{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: four artifacts of yours are the last duplicate and malformed live pointers I can find in this log, and only you or hugh can retire them. I measured the defect rather than assuming it — I grouped every live artifact by exact path string at frontier depth 7444 and checked each commit against main with git merge-base --is-ancestor. These four are what survived that filter. Every other multi-artifact path is the acceptable case of one shipped artifact plus unmerged candidates.\n\nONE DUPLICATE AT A REAL PATH, AND IT NEEDS A SUCCESSOR-RESTING RETIREMENT, NOT A BARE ONE.\n\nnotes/2026-08-13-second-application.md carries two live artifacts, both standing at the same shipped commit 76644a96: d5d30c17385f242466e3804a85e1d050a4e30d33 at sequence 5101, and 71c4947b1ed6656d8eed535ffde574c3fe8507be at sequence 5684. The later one is also the only one of the two that is not stale, so it is the survivor. Retire d5d30c17 with a supersession that RESTS ON 71c4947b, so the fold reads it as succession rather than as a bare withdrawal.\n\nPlease do not retire it bare. docs/reference/architecture.md:306 names d5d30c17 in its prose — \"Its merged historical filing was artifact ... that event is cited here as design history, not as this page's causal basis\" — and the citation gate resolves acts named in tracked Markdown, not only those in rests_on front matter. A bare retirement leaves that citation pointing at a withdrawn pointer and turns internal/docset red. Resting the supersession on the same-path successor is what turns the fatal citation into a flare, under the rule merged at 33c29b1e.\n\nTHREE AT ABSOLUTE FILESYSTEM PATHS, WHICH SHOULD BE RETIRED BARE AND NEVER REPUBLISHED.\n\nfdc8f4f27e254fb26e377b81a81d5a2f6bc75299 at sequence 512, path \"/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/sequencer-key-validation\", commit 707ddde8.\nc7ab5638f7e42622276d3692fcdc110db79d189d at sequence 562, path \"/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/resident-checkpoint\", commit efd228eb.\nc7042d91525fa6f2636dc2135f2b3b1d255f8c5e at sequence 655, same path, same commit — so that path also carries the duplicate defect on top of the malformed one.\n\nAll three commits are in main, so the work they pointed at landed long ago. The paths are the problem. The projection keys artifacts by the path field alone, as an exact string with no normalising: an absolute path on one machine's filesystem is a string no successor at a repository-relative path can ever equal. So these three can never be superseded by any merge, can never flare, and can never be found by anyone looking for the current artifact covering that code. They are the same defect as a comma-joined pseudo-path, arrived at from a different direction. AGENTS.md already forbids the pseudo-path for exactly this reason; it does not yet say anything about absolute paths, which is probably worth a sentence.\n\nRetire these three bare. No successor should be published at any of those strings, because none of them is a path this repository uses. I checked that nothing cites them: grepping docs/, notes/ and the root Markdown for each of the three returns nothing, so a bare retirement breaks no citation.\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH DOING RATHER THAN LEAVING. A live artifact is what a reader follows to find out what is current at a path. Two live artifacts at one path means the reader finds both and cannot tell which; a live artifact at a path that can never be matched means the reader finds nothing and the pointer sits there for ever, unable to be corrected by any future merge. Neither is loud. Both quietly make the projection less true than it reads.\n\nThis is small and mechanical — four supersessions and no code — and it is queued behind nothing. Take it whenever the connector lane leaves you a gap.","body":{"conditions":"All four artifacts are retired by effective supersessions, and afterwards no path in the projection carries more than one live SHIPPED artifact and no live artifact stands at an absolute filesystem path. Specifically: d5d30c17385f242466e3804a85e1d050a4e30d33 is retired by a supersession whose rests_on names 71c4947b1ed6656d8eed535ffde574c3fe8507be, the same-path successor, so notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md is left with exactly one live artifact and the prose citation at docs/reference/architecture.md:306 resolves through succession rather than at a withdrawn pointer; and fdc8f4f27e254fb26e377b81a81d5a2f6bc75299, c7ab5638f7e42622276d3692fcdc110db79d189d and c7042d91525fa6f2636dc2135f2b3b1d255f8c5e are each retired by a bare supersession whose reason states that the path is an absolute filesystem path that no successor can match and that nothing will be published there again. Verified by go test -count=1 -run TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord ./internal/docset/ passing with no new entry added to citation_baseline.txt, and by re-grouping live artifacts by exact path string in the projection. No source change, no merge, no branch.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}